Package: sensor
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Hasnain Syed <hasnain786syed@gmail.com>
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.38), libgcc-s1 (>= 4.2), libstdc++6 (>= 13), libasound2t64 (>= 1.2.11), wl-clipboard
Homepage: https://sensor.filamentplatform.com
Description: Hold a key, speak, text appears in the focused app
 Local voice dictation for Linux. Audio never leaves the machine: speech is
 transcribed on-device by whisper.cpp with the model held resident, so the
 text lands about 700ms after the key is released.
 .
 Reads the hotkey from /dev/input and types through /dev/uinput, which is the
 only route that works under Wayland as well as X11 -- Wayland deliberately
 forbids applications from reading global keys or synthesising keystrokes.
 Installing therefore adds you to the 'input' and 'uinput' groups; removing
 the package reverses that. See /usr/share/doc/sensor/README.Debian.
